<title>CANADA: Royal Bank Canada Q1 loan losses fall.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank Canada Q1 loan losses fall.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Bank of Canada said on Wednesday its first-quarter loan loss provisions for 1997 fell to C$95 million from C$110 million last year.</p>
<p>Canada's biggest bank said its estimated provision for credit losses in the year is down 14 percent to C$380 million from C$440 million in 1996.</p>
<p>Royal said net impaired loans fell 45 percent C$287 million from C$524 million in the first quarter of last year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
